;; Exemptions for `bb check:vulns` (BOU-451, BOU-618).
;;
;; Every entry MUST carry a `:why`; the gate rejects one without it.
;;
;; `:alias` excuses a finding only when every use of that library version comes
;; through the alias, so the same advisory on code that ships is still
;; reported. Prefer it to `:id`, which excuses an advisory everywhere.
;;
;; These are tools that never reach a classpath an application runs on, each at
;; its latest release, with nothing newer to move to. Look again when one
;; publishes a new version.

{:allow
 [{:alias ":build"
   :why   "Publishing only. slipset/deps-deploy 0.2.5 (latest) loads s3-wagon-private 1.3.5 at require time, which brings logback 1.0.12, aws-java-sdk-s3, jackson 2.12, jetty-http 9.4 and ion-java. Excluding it stops deps-deploy loading; we publish to Clojars, never S3."}
  {:alias ":clj-kondo"
   :why   "Linting only. clj-kondo 2026.08.04 (latest) bundles jackson-core 2.17.0 and reads no untrusted input."}
  {:alias ":outdated"
   :why   "Dependency report only. olical/depot 2.4.1 (latest) brings plexus-utils 3.4.1."}]}
